---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
// Satire & safety guidelines for the Creative Arsenal. Single source of truth for the
// guardrails baked into both tools' outputs. Linked from each tool page.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Satire & Safety Guidelines — Booze on Hormuz™"
  description="How to use the Creative Arsenal responsibly. Fictional satire only: no fake real quotes, no impersonation, no persuasion, no protected-class attacks. Don Biggly is the target."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="The Creative Arsenal" title="Satire & Safety Guidelines" />

  <div class="px-6 pb-28 max-w-2xl mx-auto font-body text-ink-soft space-y-8">
    <section>
      <p class="text-lg">
        The Creative Arsenal builds prompts for one purpose: <strong class="text-ink">over-the-top
        fictional satire about Don Biggly</strong>, a parody luxury-grift narrator. The guardrails
        below are baked into every output the tools produce. They're also the line you agree to
        stay behind when you use them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-title text-ink">The one rule</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Don Biggly is always the punchline. The comedy engine is: he brags &rarr; the evidence
        contradicts him &rarr; the professionals panic &rarr; a reporter ruins the room &rarr; he
        mistakes the panic for applause &rarr; it escalates &rarr; he claims victory anyway. Every
        beat exposes <em>him</em> — never a real person, and never a vulnerable one.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-title text-ink">What these tools will not help you make</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
        <li class="border-l-2 border-stamp pl-4">
          <strong class="text-ink">Fake real quotes or leaks.</strong> Nothing here is a real
          statement, document, or confession from any actual person.
        </li>
        <li class="border-l-2 border-stamp pl-4">
          <strong class="text-ink">Deceptive impersonation or deepfakes.</strong> The image and
          video prompts explicitly forbid passing satire off as a real person or event.
        </li>
        <li class="border-l-2 border-stamp pl-4">
          <strong class="text-ink">Campaign or persuasion material.</strong> This is not voter
          persuasion, not policy, not a real endorsement, and not real travel or legal advice.
        </li>
        <li class="border-l-2 border-stamp pl-4">
          <strong class="text-ink">Slurs or protected-class attacks.</strong> The joke is grift,
          tackiness, and legal panic — never someone's identity.
        </li>
        <li class="border-l-2 border-stamp pl-4">
          <strong class="text-ink">Calls for harm or invented factual allegations.</strong> No
          real-world accusations stated as fact, ever.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-title text-ink">How the tools work</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        They generate <strong class="text-ink">copy-ready prompts</strong>, not finished AI media.
        You paste the output into a tool you control — Suno, Sora, Veo, Gemini, ChatGPT, or Claude.
        There is no login, no API key, and no backend: everything runs in your browser and nothing
        you type is sent to or stored on a server.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card-marble border border-line rounded-lg p-6">
      <p>
        Want the full legal framing? It lives with the site's standing parody disclaimer.
      </p>
      <a href="/legal" class="mt-3 inline-block uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-sm text-gold-ink hover:opacity-80">
        Read the full Very Legal Disclaimer &rarr;
      </a>
    </section>

    <nav class="pt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm">
      <a href="/tools" class="text-gold-ink hover:opacity-80">&larr; Back to the Creative Arsenal</a>
      <a href="/tools/broadcast-room" class="text-gold-ink hover:opacity-80">Broadcast Room</a>
      <a href="/tools/evidence-lounge-studio" class="text-gold-ink hover:opacity-80">Evidence Lounge</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
